name stress_pose
describe The worst pose measured so far: ground level at a hilltop, shadows and AO on, looking out over the terrain. CLAUDE.md records 76 fps here against 155-159 panoramic, so this -- not the panorama -- is the pose a GPU budget is set from. Used by goals 220 and 221 as the instrumentation-cost measurement pose.
backend both

# TAA off for every scenario that compares a capture against a golden. Measured, not assumed:
# with TAA on, vk-vs-vk moves 0.996% of pixels at this pose against a 1.5% gate, and with it off
# 0.341% -- see dev/harness/src/image_compare.hpp for the full four-case table.
option --no-taa

pose_ground 48,0 -90 -6 1.7
wait 5

capture end stress_pose

assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6

# ------------------------------------------------- Prompt 005 goal 291: the ALIASING gate
# A DIFFERENT question from contrast_percent above, and the two move in opposite directions:
# contrast_percent asks "is there texture", moire_ratio asks "how much of that texture is
# energy piled against the pixel Nyquist limit rather than spread over resolvable
# frequencies". A deliberate stipple raises the first and leaves the second alone; aliasing
# raises both. Gate on both or a change that trades one for the other passes unnoticed.
#
# CALIBRATED, and this metric is far tighter than the GPU-time gate above because it is a
# DETERMINISTIC IMAGE MEASUREMENT rather than a clock reading -- no boost state, no
# contention. Three consecutive runs:
#   measured 1.843, spread under 0.05%
#   with --no-filter-albedo (goal 278 off): 3.814
# The gate is 2.2 -- about 1.2x the measured value, and it FAILS at 3.814, which is
# goal 291's own falsification and was verified by running it rather than assumed.
assert moire_ratio < 2.2

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ goal 273: the regression gate
# A PERCENTILE of the GPU timestamp range across this fixed camera path, per research section 6.8 --
# never a mean (one hitch moves it) and above all never fps, which this machine's 165 Hz
# FIFO_RELAXED panel caps at 155-159 and which therefore cannot express a regression at all.
#
# PER BACKEND, because vk and d3d12 differ by 30-35% here and `ctest -L scenario` runs vk ONLY. A
# single threshold would have to be set by the slower backend, leaving the faster one 35% of slack
# -- a 30% vk regression would sail straight through the gate that CI actually runs.
#
# TWO METRICS, and the reason is a measured failure of the first one-metric version (goal 273b,
# log section 28). A single `gpu_ms_p95 < 4.4` gate FLAKED: nine consecutive standalone runs put p95
# at 3.667-3.687 ms (a 0.3% spread), but the same scenario inside a full 333-test `ctest` measured
# 4.511 and failed, roughly one run in three. The frame histogram of the failing run is bimodal --
# 267 of 551 frames pacing at 11-16 ms with 15-18 ms `present` -- so what moved was the machine's
# state, not the renderer. The MEDIAN of that same failing run was 3.49 ms, indistinguishable from
# the 3.50 measured standalone.
#
# So the median carries the regression signal and the p95 guards the tail:
#   * gpu_ms_median is set at ~1.15x the measured value. It is the FALSIFIABLE gate -- tightening
#     it by 20% fails, which is goal 273's own Check, and it is robust to suite contention because
#     contention moves the tail and leaves the median alone.
#   * gpu_ms_p95 is set above the worst value observed INCLUDING under full-suite contention. It is
#     deliberately loose: it catches a large tail regression without flaking. It is not falsifiable
#     at 20% and is not claimed to be.
#
# PER BACKEND, because vk and d3d12 differ by 30-35% here and `ctest -L scenario` runs vk ONLY. A
# single threshold would have to be set by the slower backend, leaving the faster one 35% of slack
# -- a 30% vk regression would sail straight through the gate that CI actually runs.
#
# Measured 2026-09-07 on the shipping build (goal 258's palette included), three runs each:
#   vk    median 3.49 3.49 3.50 3.50 3.50 4.01 4.13 4.14   p95 3.68 3.70 3.71 3.72 3.73 4.38 4.39
#                                                                4.43 4.51
#
# AND THE REASON vk's OWN RANGE IS 18% WIDE, which took a while to find because nothing in the
# frame data shows it: THE GPU's POWER STATE MOVES IT. Twelve runs early in the session sat at
# 3.49-3.50 ms; three hours of continuous GPU load later the same binary at the same pose measured
# 4.01-4.14, and `nvidia-smi` sampled DURING a run reads 2445 MHz of a 3105 MHz maximum at 23 W
# with no thermal-slowdown flag set -- a lower boost state, not throttling. 3.50/4.13 = 84.7%,
# 2445/3105 = 78.7%: the clock explains essentially all of it.
#
# So an ABSOLUTE millisecond threshold on this machine has an ~18% noise floor that belongs to the
# laptop, not the renderer, and every number below is set from the full range INCLUDING the low
# power state. Goal 273's 20%-tightening Check was performed and passed (measured 3.495 against a
# tightened 3.2), but it was performed in the high state -- it is a check at a moment, not an
# invariant, and saying otherwise would be overclaiming. The real fix is a clock-independent
# metric; `mean_primary_steps` already exists in the ramp path and goal 275e is to make it a
# scenario assertion.
#   d3d12 median 5.50 5.51 5.52 5.60 5.66 6.05 6.06 6.10 6.44 6.51 6.59
#         p95    5.97 6.16 6.41 6.62 6.99 7.10 8.32
#
# AND THE d3d12 GATE IS NOT FALSIFIABLE AT 20%, which is stated rather than papered over. Ten runs
# spread 5.50-6.51 ms -- 18% -- with consecutive runs 15% apart (6.507 then 5.658, back to back).
# A spread wider than the 20% tightening margin means no single threshold can both survive the
# spread and fail when tightened by 20%: 20% below any gate that clears 6.51 is 5.21, which the
# 5.50 runs pass. So d3d12's gate is a REGRESSION GUARD ONLY, set 10% above the worst observed.
# Goal 273's falsification Check is carried by vk -- which is the backend `ctest -L scenario`
# actually runs -- where ten runs spread 0.3% and the same tightening fails every time.
assert gpu_ms_median < 4.8 vk
assert gpu_ms_median < 7.2 d3d12
assert gpu_ms_p95 < 5.2 vk
assert gpu_ms_p95 < 10.0 d3d12
